<title>USA: G7 finance ministers, central bankers start talks.</title>
<headline>G7 finance ministers, central bankers start talks.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finance ministers and central bank governors of the Group of Seven industrial nations started meeting in Washington shortly after noon (1600 GMT) Sunday.</p>
<p>The talks, grouping officials from the United States, Japan, Germany, France, Britain, Canada and Italy, are expected to last all afternoon, and U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin is due to brief the press at around 1800 EST (2200 GMT), officials said.</p>
</text>
